WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:14.956
Lara and Mom walked along a canal.

2
00:00:14.957 --> 00:00:18.509
Mom read aloud from her Venice guidebook.

3
00:00:18.510 --> 00:00:28.407
But Lara was too excited to listen.

4
00:00:28.407 --> 00:00:32.791
"This is the Rialto Bridge," read Mom.

5
00:00:32.792 --> 00:00:37.122
"It is the oldest bridge on the Grand Canal and—"

6
00:00:37.122 --> 00:00:44.336
"Ooh!" Lara squealed. She pointed to a row of black boats.

7
00:00:44.336 --> 00:00:48.503
"Mom, can we take a gondola ride?"

8
00:00:48.503 --> 00:00:55.221
"Good idea," said Mom. "My feet are getting sore."

9
00:00:55.221 --> 00:00:59.460
Mom hired a gondola to go to St. Mark's Square.

10
00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:05.452
Marco, the driver, helped them into the boat.

11
00:01:05.452 --> 00:01:14.571
Lara and Mom sat down on the pretty red cushions.

12
00:01:14.571 --> 00:01:19.110
Marco gestured with one arm and rowed with the other.

13
00:01:19.110 --> 00:01:26.911
"This is the Grand Canal. It's one of the major waterways in Venice," he said.

14
00:01:26.912 --> 00:01:29.773
"It's almost four kilometers long.

15
00:01:29.773 --> 00:01:34.448
And it's ninety meters wide in some places.

16
00:01:34.448 --> 00:01:40.089
There are 177 canals in Venice."

17
00:01:40.089 --> 00:01:45.512
A long motorboat passed by.

18
00:01:45.512 --> 00:01:49.379
"That looks like a bus!" said Lara.

19
00:01:49.386 --> 00:01:52.605
"That's a water bus," said Marco.

20
00:01:52.605 --> 00:01:55.051
"We don't have cars in Venice.

21
00:01:55.051 --> 00:01:58.084
So people have to walk.

22
00:01:58.085 --> 00:02:00.601
Or they travel on the canals.

23
00:02:00.601 --> 00:02:04.331
We have water buses and even water taxis!"

24
00:02:04.331 --> 00:02:09.949
He pointed to a smaller motorboat.

25
00:02:09.949 --> 00:02:17.468
Marco steered the gondola into a narrow canal.

26
00:02:17.469 --> 00:02:21.708
"There's less traffic in this canal," Lara said.

27
00:02:21.708 --> 00:02:27.490
She stared up at the tall, elegant buildings.

28
00:02:27.490 --> 00:02:33.940
"Venice was a rich and powerful city during the Renaissance," Marco said.

29
00:02:33.940 --> 00:02:38.403
"People built palace-like houses to show off their wealth."

30
00:02:38.403 --> 00:02:42.784
They passed under a covered white bridge.

31
00:02:42.784 --> 00:02:47.166
"The Doge’s Palace is on the right," Marco said.

32
00:02:47.166 --> 00:02:51.845
It was a beautiful white building.

33
00:02:51.845 --> 00:02:54.678
Lara wrinkled her nose.

34
00:02:54.679 --> 00:02:58.568
"What's a doge?" she asked.

35
00:02:58.568 --> 00:03:03.060
"The doge was the ruler of Venice," Marco said.

36
00:03:03.060 --> 00:03:05.877
"The palace is a museum now."

37
00:03:05.877 --> 00:03:16.174
At the end of the canal, Marco turned the gondola into an open lagoon.

38
00:03:16.175 --> 00:03:18.793
"Here we are," announced Marco.

39
00:03:18.793 --> 00:03:23.598
"This is St. Mark's Square!"

40
00:03:23.598 --> 00:03:28.012
Marco helped Mom and Lara out of the gondola.

41
00:03:28.012 --> 00:03:32.780
"Can we go see the Doge's Palace, Mom?" asked Lara.

42
00:03:32.780 --> 00:03:38.156
"Be sure to see St. Mark's Church and the bell tower too!" Marco said.

43
00:03:38.156 --> 00:03:42.579
"Thank you," said Mom. She turned to Lara.

44
00:03:42.579 --> 00:03:47.729
"My feet feel rested now. I'm ready for more sightseeing."

45
00:03:47.729 --> 00:03:55.551
Lara cheered. "Good! Let's go!"

